    "text": "© 2026 SaturdayDownSouth.com Home > News > Sports > How to Watch Arkansas vs Arizona: TV Channel, Time, & Postseason Stream Details Ad Disclosure This article/post contains references to products or services from one or more of our advertisers or partners. We may receive compensation when you click on links to those products or services. The No. 14 Arkansas Razorbacks face the No. 2 Arizona Wildcats in an important 2025 postseason matchup. Both programs enter this neutral site game riding momentum from their respective conference tournaments. Arizona holds a 2-0 postseason record in the Big 12 standings and an impressive 32-2 overall mark under head coach Tommy Lloyd. Meanwhile, John Calipari and his Arkansas squad bring a 26-8 overall record and a matching 2-0 postseason standing in the SEC. Watch Arkansas vs Arizona on Paramount+. This game centers on two top 15 AP ranked teams clashing in California as both rosters look to advance their postseason runs. As the Wildcats and Razorbacks prepare to meet on the court, fans will want to know exactly how to follow the action. Continue reading for all the essential broadcast details, including the scheduled tip time, the exact location, the national TV channel, and how to access streaming options for this matchup. When is the Arkansas vs Arizona Game? What Time Does it Start? The postseason matchup between the Arkansas Razorbacks and Arizona Wildcats is scheduled for March 26, 2026. Tip time is set for 9:45 PM ET. Where is the Arkansas vs Arizona Game? This postseason matchup is being played at the SAP Center at San Jose in San Jose, California. Because this is a neutral site event, the Arizona Wildcats are officially designated as the home team, while the Arkansas Razorbacks will serve as the away team. How can I Watch the Arkansas vs Arizona game? The postseason matchup between the Arkansas Razorbacks and the Arizona Wildcats will be broadcast nationally on television. Viewers can watch the game live by tuning in directly to CBS. Fans planning to follow the event should check their local television listings for the specific CBS network affiliate carrying the broadcast in their area. How can I Stream the Arkansas vs Arizona game? Since the matchup between the Arkansas Razorbacks and Arizona Wildcats is airing on CBS, viewers can stream the live broadcast directly through Paramount+. The network provides a live feed of the local CBS broadcast for subscribers on its premium tier. In addition to Paramount+, fans have several other live TV streaming options that carry CBS. Viewers planning to use one of these platforms to stream the game should confirm that the local CBS station is available in their specific regional market prior to tip. Paramount+ – Direct live feed of the CBS broadcast (premium tier required) FuboTV – Includes local CBS affiliates in standard channel packages Sling – Includes local CBS affiliates in standard channel packages YouTube TV – Includes local CBS affiliates in standard channel packages Hulu + Live TV – Includes local CBS affiliates in standard channel packages DIRECTV STREAM – Includes local CBS affiliates in standard channel packages Who Will Win the Arkansas vs Arizona Game? Data from Kalshi on March 24th. Based on the latest Kalshi prediction market data, the Arizona Wildcats are projected as the favored team. Forecasters currently give the Wildcats a 76% implied probability of securing the victory. The Arkansas Razorbacks enter the contest as the underdog, with market predictions reflecting a 24% implied probability of winning. These percentages indicate that prediction market participants consider Arizona significantly more likely to advance in this matchup. Creative Manager and Writer at Sportradar. Craig has previously worked as a camera operator and video director in radio and television, as well as a content coordinator in the non-profit sector. You might also like...",
